.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt PDP11 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pdp11
.Nd attach to the PiDP-11 console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches to the console of the simulated PDP-11.
The console runs as a
.Xr screen 1
session named
.Ar pidp11
in the background, so the PDP-11 does not notice when
.Nm
detaches.
The console follows the terminal you call
.Nm
from: call it from a login prompt, a remote
.Xr ssh 1
session or a desktop terminal and it appears there.
.Pp
When the packaged system services are installed the screen session belongs
to the
.Ar pidp11
service account.
.Nm
then joins it through
.Xr sudo 8
(see
.Pa /etc/sudoers.d/pidp11 )
so that several users can share the console at once.
Otherwise it takes over the session belonging to the calling user.
.Pp
If no session is running,
.Nm
prints
.Dq PiDP-11 is not running
on stderr and exits 1; start the simulator service first.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Call it from a fresh login to get the PDP-11 console in that terminal:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pdp11
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr screen 1 ,
.Xr pidp11-sty 1 ,
.Xr pidp11-install-systems 1 ,
.Xr vt05 1 ,
.Xr tek4010 1
